{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS3MY51KKiS24FGXB4of","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VwJMB7rcYYvDoegzvjktFG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-b4wZwA; python3 - <<'E'\ns=open('server.py').read()\ns=s.replace('''DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL = 3600   # seconds; used when the provider does not say how long a token lives\n''','')\ns=s.replace('''    expires_in = int(tok.get(\"expires_in\") or DEFAULT_TOKEN_TTL)\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n    if not refresh:\n        log(f\"{user_id}: no refresh_token in response, scheduling expiry in {expires_in}s\")\n''','''    # Intervals tokens have no refresh_token/expires_in: valid until the athlete revokes them.\n    expires_in = tok.get(\"expires_in\")\n    refresh = tok.get(\"refresh_token\")\n''')\ns=s.replace('''\"expires_at\": time.time() + expires_in, \"status\"''','''\"expires_at\": time.time() + int(expires_in) if expires_in else None, \"status\"''')\ns=s.replace('(expires in {expires_in}s)\")','(no expiry)\")')\ns=s.replace('''if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:''','''if c[\"status\"] != \"connected\" or c[\"expires_at\"] is None or c[\"expires_at\"] - now > 300:''')\ns=s.replace('''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n''','')\ns=s.replace('''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/disconnect\":''','''        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/auth/init\":\n            return self.auth_init()\n        if url.path == \"/api/intervals/disconnect\":''')\ns=s.replace('''        self.redirect(AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\"))''','''        self.send_json(200, {\"authorize_url\": AUTHORIZE_URL + \"?\" + urllib.parse.urlencode(params, safe=\":,\")})''')\ns=s.replace(\"# Step 1: build the authorize URL and send the browser to Intervals.\",\"# Step 1: authenticated POST (XHR); returns the authorize URL for the SPA to navigate to.\")\ns=s.replace('''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})''','''        except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n            if e.code == 401:  # revoked on the Intervals side\n                with LOCK:\n                    c.update(status=\"expired, reconnect\", access_token=None)\n                return self.send_json(409, {\"error\": \"intervals not connected\"})\n            self.send_json(e.code, {\"error\": f\"intervals returned {e.code}\"})''')\nopen('server.py','w').write(s)\nc=open('config.py').read()\nc=c.replace('\"ACTIVITY:READ,ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"','\"ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE\"  # each area once; :WRITE implies :READ')\nopen('config.py','w').write(c)\na=open('static/app.js').read()\na=a.replace('''<a class=\"btn\" href=\"/api/intervals/auth/init\">Connect Intervals.icu</a>''','''<button class=\"btn\" id=\"connect\">Connect Intervals.icu</button>''')\na=a.replace('''    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''','''    const cn = document.getElementById(\"connect\");\n    if (cn) cn.onclick = async () => {\n      try {\n        const { authorize_url } = await api(\"/api/intervals/auth/init\", { method: \"POST\" });\n        window.location.assign(authorize_url);\n      } catch (e) { root.innerHTML = `<p class=\"card\">Error: ${esc(e.message)}</p>`; }\n    };\n    const d = document.getElementById(\"disconnect\");''')\nopen('static/app.js','w').write(a)\nE\npython3 -c \"import ast;ast.parse(open('server.py').read())\"; git diff --stat\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Intervals.icu connection: causes and fixes\n\n## Causes\n1. **Connect always 401'd (every athlete).** The button was a plain link to `GET /api/intervals/auth/init`. A full-page navigation doesn't send the `Authorization: Bearer` header, which the SPA only attaches via `fetch`. Fix: init is now an authenticated `POST` returning `{authorize_url}`. The SPA calls it with `fetch` and then runs `window.location.assign(...)` (`server.py`, `static/app.js`).\n2. **Authorize URL returned 400 `invalid_request` (the hand-pasted link, since 2026-10-02).** The calendar-sync change added `CALENDAR:READ` and `ACTIVITY:READ` next to the `:WRITE` scopes. Intervals rejects an area named twice, because `:WRITE` implies `:READ`. The 400 body doesn't name the parameter, and I couldn't reach Intervals to confirm. This is the best fit for the symptoms. Fix: `ACTIVITY:WRITE,WELLNESS:READ,CALENDAR:WRITE` (`config.py`).\n3. **Rivera's token \"expired\" after an hour.** Intervals tokens have no `refresh_token` and no `expires_in`. They last until the athlete revokes them. The code invented a 3600s default TTL, and the refresher then marked the connection expired. Fix: no invented expiry (`expires_at` is `None` unless the provider sends one), and the refresher skips such tokens. Revocation is now handled lazily: a 401 from Intervals marks the connection \"expired, reconnect\".\n\n## Colleague's note\n- **Applied:** point 1 (no refresh/expiry, handle 401 lazily), point 2 (no duplicate scopes), point 4 (POST init plus `window.location.assign`).\n- **Not applied:**\n  - Dropping `grant_type` and `redirect_uri` from the token exchange. Rivera's logged exchange succeeded with them, so I left it alone.\n  - JWT `state` and the account-mismatch guard. The existing HMAC-signed state with a 15-minute TTL already carries the user identity.\n  - Encrypting the token at rest. The store is in-memory here, and prod storage isn't in this repo.\n\n## Not verified\nI couldn't test against the real Intervals.icu. I only syntax-checked `server.py`. I didn't run the server or the browser flow.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5391,"cache_read_input_tokens":24334,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input